            <div xml:id="d303">

                <pb facs="0400" n="302" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg302"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">738.3915/206: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé des Affaires in the Dominican Republic</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Brewer</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-03-01T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 1, 1920—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>9. Department informed that Haitian Government has advised its Minister Santo
                    Domingo to inform Dominican Government that it is prepared to enter into <hi
                        rendition="#italic">pourparlers</hi> relative to boundary question. Confer
                    with Military Government and report at once whether Haitian Minister is
                    empowered to discuss this matter on the lines of note from Dominican Foreign
                    Office of December 22 to him proposing arbitration of whole question by the Pope
                    or whether Haitian Minister has been instructed to discuss direct settlement of
                    the boundary dispute.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
